# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# Every text blob is stored LF in the repository (the index already is —
# verified with `git ls-files --eol`). Windows working trees still get
# CRLF on checkout via core.autocrlf, but the *committed* bytes — which
# is what Linux and Windows CI both hash, diff, and feed to golden
# fixtures — are identical on every platform. Without this file that
# guarantee rests only on each contributor's local core.autocrlf, which
# is exactly how a CRLF blob slips into history and makes Windows and
# Linux CI disagree on the same commit.
* text=auto
# scaffold/ and assets/ are compiled into the binary with include_str!, so their
# checkout bytes ARE the binary's bytes. Without a pinned eol, a Windows CI or
# release build (core.autocrlf=true) embedded CRLF and `albedo init` wrote
# different files than the Linux build of the same commit
# (build_artifact_local_data failed on windows-latest only). Listed BEFORE the
# binary patterns below so `*.ico binary` etc. still win (later lines override).
scaffold/** text eol=lf
assets/**   text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never apply EOL conversion or attempt a text diff.
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.node  binary
*.tgz   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
*.bin   binary

# Windows shell scripts require CRLF to run correctly.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
